<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Carlist War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1872">1872</a>–<a href="/years/1876">1876</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third Carlist War of 1872–1876 was a civil war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in which supporters of the pretender Carlos VII tried to win the throne. The Carlists built a state with its own administration in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>, the Basque provinces and parts of Catalonia, fighting the governments of Amadeo I, the First Spanish Republic and the restored monarchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-xii">Alfonso XII</a>, which defeated them in 1876.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/third-carlist-war.jpg" alt="Third Carlist War" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francisco Oller y Cestero (1833-1917) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bataille_de_Trevi%C3%B1o.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
